From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 02:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: Limit the PS5 pointer by a swapchain window's place
 on the real screen.

The pointer stays in the client area of the window whose swapchain last
presented. The server keeps the pointer in real screen pixels, but that
client area was read in the game's coordinates, so the two agree only
while no display mode is set. Under a mode the game sets, the limit is
the mode's size in real pixels: a game at 1024x768 had its pointer stop
at (1024, 768) of a 1920x1080 screen, about 55% across and 72% down the
image, and could not reach the buttons beyond. The client area is now
mapped to real pixels, for the limit and for the place given to the
hardware cursor.
---
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
index 3ab645a..d273970 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
@@ -927,6 +927,9 @@ void ps5drv_vulkan_cursor( void *vulkan_handle, HWND hwnd )
     BOOL placed = hwnd && get_window_rects( hwnd, COORDS_SCREEN, &rects, get_dpi_for_window( hwnd ) ) &&
                   rects.client.right > rects.client.left && rects.client.bottom > rects.client.top;
 
+    /* the pointer's place is the server's, so its limits are too: a display mode
+     * smaller than the desktop gives the window another size there */
+    if (placed) rects = map_window_rects_virt_to_raw( rects, get_dpi_for_window( hwnd ) );
     if (!looked)
     {
         looked = TRUE;
